     zzffss pprroojjeecctt [--dd|--rr] _f_i_l_e|_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_yâ¦
       List project identifier (ID) and inherit flag of files and directories.

       --dd  Show the directory project ID and inherit flag, not its children.

       --rr  List subdirectories recursively.

     zzffss pprroojjeecctt --CC [--kkrr] _f_i_l_e|_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_yâ¦
       Clear project inherit flag and/or ID on the files and directories.

       --kk  Keep the project ID unchanged.  If not specified, the project ID
           will be reset to zero.

       --rr  Clear subdirectories' flags recursively.

     zzffss pprroojjeecctt --cc [--00] [--dd|--rr] [--pp _i_d] _f_i_l_e|_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_yâ¦
       Check project ID and inherit flag on the files and directories: report
       entries without the project inherit flag, or with project IDs different
       from the target directory's project ID or the one specified with --pp.

       --00     Delimit filenames with a NUL byte instead of newline, don't out‐
              put diagnoses.

       --dd     Check the directory project ID and inherit flag, not its chil‐
              dren.

       --pp _i_d  Compare to _i_d instead of the target files and directories'
              project IDs.

       --rr     Check subdirectories recursively.

     zzffss pprroojjeecctt --pp _i_d [--rrss] _f_i_l_e|_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_yâ¦
       Set project ID and/or inherit flag on the files and directories.

       --pp _i_d  Set the project ID to the given value.

       --rr     Set on subdirectories recursively.

       --ss     Set project inherit flag on the given files and directories.
              This is usually used for setting up tree quotas with --rr.  In
              that case, the directory's project ID will be set for all its
              descendants, unless specified explicitly with --pp.

